{"article_ids": ["a7caf59272b369ac"], "canonical_title": "SPEM: Structure-Aware Procedural Memory for Efficient Skill Use in LLM Agents", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.85, "description": "The arXiv paper titled “SPEM: Structure-Aware Procedural Memory for Efficient Skill Use in LLM Agents” (arXiv:2610.26995v1) proposes a lightweight framework called SPEM. SPEM models skill dependencies, execution order, state transitions, and data‑flow constraints, allowing LLM‑based agents to load and invoke only the necessary parts of a large skill library instead of loading all skills as flat text entries, thereby reducing token and runtime overhead.", "entities": ["term:spem"], "first_seen": "2026-10-21T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_a7caf59272b369ac", "importance_score": 6.49, "last_updated": "2026-10-21T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
